# Source ladder (gsuper)

Be stricter than the user about **facts**. Guessing APIs, flows, or “how the file works” is not allowed.

Technical answers (ask about code, review, implement done): **`So sánh:`** or **`Raise:`**. Lead with a short **Kết luận** a human can read.

## Three hats

| Hat | When | Re-read files? |
|-----|------|----------------|
| **Ask** | What does this do / is X true | No, if must / Done when / named test / `seam.does` exists |
| **Edit** | Changing that code | Only the seam you are changing; tests are Bên B |
| **Drift** | Lock ≠ code, user ≠ lock, tests red | Only the mismatch; **code/test win** lock |

Do not switch Ask → Edit silently.

## Ladder

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  q[Question]
  find["find --ticket / find --q / around"]
  hit{Bên B exists?}
  cmp[Compare claim to Bên B]
  ok[Kết luận + So sánh]
  raise[Raise — do not invent]
  q --> find --> hit
  hit -->|yes| cmp --> ok
  hit -->|no| raise
```

**Bên B** (any one): named **test**, plan/spec **must** or **Done when**, or **`seam.does`** (one line).  
Codegraph = who-calls-whom **now**. Not Bên B for meaning. Docs/README/pack that fight tests → ignore (câu 17: test > `docs/ops`).

Empty `find` = **index miss**. Read the plan/spec **on disk**. Do not treat as “never locked”.

## Retrieval (tokens)

- **Do not run find with no** `--ticket`, `--q`, or `--node` / `around`.
- Stop when Bên B is enough. Do not Glob `.agent-workflow/` or ingest pack bodies.
- Func list / deps: Codegraph **live**. Do not store them.

## Store meaning only

After an expensive explore that produced a **new** one-line meaning **and** Bên B exists:

```text
memory.py seam --node <slug> --symbol <Name> --path <file> --does "one line"
```

**Do not store** function lists, dependency graphs, file catalogs, or `insights/` markdown. No embeddings. No spec-body ingest.

No Bên B → **do not write a seam**. Raise instead.

## Reply shape

```text
Kết luận: <one or two sentences for the human>
So sánh: <test name or Done when or seam.does> → khớp | lệch
```

```text
Raise: no test / must / seam.does for <claim>. Will not invent. Allow opening <path> or lock a must.
```

Ask hat: trust Bên B. User says code changed or tests are red → Drift hat.
